 ## 2026-08-11
 
+### 2015 — libssh2 M0 matrix passes while external and aggregate gates stay red (TASK-260715-1u2vpc)
+- MATRIX: The real-loopback-sshd libssh2 gate passes 46 tests across adapter, bridge, and provider-contract suites. A new test-only compatibility row forces and verifies both approved transport sets: curve25519/Ed25519/aes256-ctr/hmac-sha2-256 and group14-sha256/P-256/aes128-ctr/hmac-sha2-512. Client byte/time/manual rekey, server-rekey-safe traffic, keepalive transmission, direct/exec/upload, bounded pressure, cancellation, privacy, and zero-owned-resource cleanup pass.
+- DEFERRED GAPS: Receive-window consumer credit/cap, RFC channel-open reasons, exact exec-exit/core-dump metadata, and deep server-rekey/keepalive observability remain explicit `unsupported` or runtime `notReported`, owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`. Physical scale, memory, and soak remain separate M3 rows; no exact value was inferred from the C fixture's 16 observed server-KEX transitions.
+- VERIFICATION: libssh2 artifact/source/rekey gates, strict Swift format, four extension-safe macOS arm64/x86_64 adapter/harness builds, and affected tests exit 0. Affected adapter coverage is 80.28% regions / 93.86% functions / 90.04% lines.
+- RED GATES: Overall Gate P0 remains blocked on Apple account evidence APC34W-B1–B3 despite the accepted physical-Mac row passing; common conformance task `TASK-260715-2d3g5e` remains backlog. Full `swift test` exits 1 with five issues in two unrelated HEV UDP tests; both pass alone, preserving the aggregate-order race under focused owner `BUG-260728-2j25tu`. No review handoff or waiver is claimed.
+
 ### 1947 — SSH bootstrap diagnostics separate security gates from transient operations (TASK-260715-13labb)
 - IMPLEMENTATION: The macOS profile-driven SSH boundary now projects typed profile, path, connect, negotiation, host-policy, Keychain, public-key authentication, cancellation/user-stop, and session-close causes into the fixed `sshProfileBootstrap` provider domain. Public errors and runtime snapshots carry only stable code/stage, configuration generation, user-action category, retry disposition, and reviewed algorithm/endpoint-family context; arbitrary underlying prose and identifying values are structurally unrepresentable.
 - RETRY POLICY: Corrupt or unsupported profiles, host mismatch/change/revocation/unsupported algorithms, inaccessible or malformed credentials, and authentication rejection are terminal until configuration, trust, or credential state changes. Only bounded timeouts, unavailable paths, and an explicit allowlist of transient transport interruptions are marked `retryableLater`; this task records classification and adds no reconnect behavior.
